* DONE setup shouldn't be a capability
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-06-18 Thu 20:45
:ARCHIVE_FILE: ~/workspace/ghostore/project.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Tasks
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: project
:ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
:END:
now we have ai capability and ai setup capability? that sounds wrong. each capability should have two sides: setup and usage. the usage side should be exposed to apps, and the setup side should only be accessible to the main app, settings app should be part of the main app? or should it be an app with admin access or something.
Resolved: one capability id, two facets. Folded agentSetup into ai/admin — the
use facet (generateText) is exposed to apps, the admin facet (signIn/selectModel/
signOut/status) only to the first-party Settings app, gated host-side on appId
like the volume `system` allowlist. Settings stays an app, with admin access. See
c32a636.

* DONE unify calendar/email onto the use/admin facet pattern
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-06-18 Thu 20:45
:ARCHIVE_FILE: ~/workspace/ghostore/project.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Tasks
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: project
:ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
:END:
Apply the same use/admin split to the rest, so every capability has the same
shape: a host-owned backing store, a use facet apps call, and an admin facet only
the first-party Settings app can reach.
- integrations (list/connect/disconnect accounts) is today a standalone setup
  capability — make it the admin facet over the accounts that back calendar + email.
- note it is 1-admin-to-many-use, not 1:1: one accounts/admin surface feeds both
  calendar.listToday and email.*, so likely one shared accounts/admin facet rather
  than calendar/admin + email/admin duplicated.
- gate: each admin facet is gated on a first-party allowlist host-side (today
  systemAllowlist + aiAdminAllowlist). As more land, consider one generic admin
  gate instead of a per-capability allowlist repeated in every host.

